msgid "Unicode Character Variants"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/tools/text.rst:265
msgid ""
"These are officially defined character variants. Simple examples of these "
"include slashed 0 as an alternative to 0, but more commonly these are used "
"for Han ideographs. In particular, place and people names require certain "
"glyph variants to be used to look recognisable, and character variants "
"provide this access. Krita will only show variants that are available in the "
"font itself."
msgstr ""

